# TUI-DESIGN-3 §4 (D-K) idle: `/s` (an alias) → the /status block; typing `/s` shows the ghost arrow ` → /status`; `/p d` opens the
# decisions tab (App-local, alias- and case-aware, F3), a second `/p d` collapses it; `/budgett` (a fixable error) keeps the draft — Ctrl-C
# clears it; `/exit` leaves 0
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
sleep 0.3
# `/` and `s` are two keystrokes: `composer:palette` (keys/resolve.ts:416) opens the palette on the `/` key alone, and the
# ghost arrow is drawn only while the palette is open (App.tsx:2149) — one `send /s` write is a single input event and opens nothing
send /
expect Tab completes
send s
expect → /status
sleep 0.3
send \r
expect \[ui\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* status
sleep 0.3
send /p d
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect ▾(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* decisions
sleep 0.3
send /p d
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect ▸(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* jev|─{10}
sleep 0.3
send /budgett
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect unknown command|no such command|error
expect (?:›|>) (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*/budgett
send \x03
expect Follow-up, question|Say hi
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
